Package: easyTSA
Title: Trial Sequential Analysis for 'meta' Objects
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Vanio", "Antunes", email = "vanio.antunes.md@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Runs Trial Sequential Analysis (TSA) directly on meta-analysis
    objects created with the 'meta' package. Computes the required information
    size (heterogeneity-adjusted), the cumulative Z-curve, Lan-DeMets
    O'Brien-Fleming monitoring boundaries, futility boundaries (inner wedge)
    and TSA-adjusted confidence intervals, and draws the TSA plot with
    'ggplot2'. It also writes and reads the '.TSA' files used by the
    Copenhagen Trial Unit TSA software and can launch that program (installed
    separately, Java required), so the same analysis can be opened there.
